
# SSM-RAG Setup

## Environment
- Python 3.11
- Ubuntu / WSL2 (Windows 11)
- NVIDIA GPU with CUDA support

## Libraries and Versions

| Library | Version |
|---|---|
| PyTorch | 2.5.1+cu124 |
| Transformers | 4.47.1 |
| BitsAndBytes | 0.45.5 |
| Triton | 3.1.0 |
| Mamba-SSM | 2.2.6.post3 |
| Accelerate | Latest compatible |
| Causal-Conv1D | 1.4.0+ |
| Safetensors | Latest compatible |
| Matplotlib | Latest compatible |

## Installation

Run these commands in the Ubuntu terminal.

### 1. Create a virtual environment

sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3.11 python3.11-venv python3-pip build-essential -y

python3.11 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

python -m pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel

### 2. Install PyTorch (CUDA 12.4)

pip install torch==2.5.1 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124

### 3. Install the remaining libraries

pip install transformers==4.47.1 accelerate bitsandbytes==0.45.5 safetensors matplotlib

### 4. Install Mamba dependencies

pip install causal-conv1d>=1.4.0
pip install mamba-ssm==2.2.6.post3 --no-build-isolation

## Verify Installation

python -c "import torch; print(torch.__version__); print('CUDA:', torch.cuda.is_available())"

python -c "import transformers, bitsandbytes, mamba_ssm; print('Libraries loaded successfully')"

CUDA should return True.